Subject: [PATCH 1/3] =?UTF-8?q?feat(seasonal):=20core=20=E2=80=94=20domain?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20+=20SeasonResolver=20+=20IntervalService=20(#67,=201/3)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First commit of the seasonal-intervals feature. Storage, enums, and the
pure-logic services for resolving the current season and computing the
effective interval. No integration with next_due_at yet — that's commit
2/3; UI is 3/3. This commit alone is dormant and changes nothing about
runtime behaviour.

Storage (V17 migration):
  - users.seasonal_enabled (default false)
  - users.seasonal_mode VARCHAR(16) with CHECK IN ('MULTIPLIER','FIXED')
  - users.summer_start_mmdd / winter_start_mmdd as INT MMDD (401 = Apr 1,
    1001 = Oct 1) — pure integer comparison instead of date parsing
  - users.summer_multiplier / winter_multiplier as NUMERIC(3,2),
    defaults 0.80 / 1.20 (per issue AC)
  - users.summer_interval_override_days / winter_interval_override_days
    INTEGER nullable — for FIXED mode; null → fallback to base
  - plants.seasonal_override VARCHAR(8) CHECK IN
    ('INHERIT','ON','OFF'), default INHERIT
  - No indexes — these columns are only read in single-user / single-plant
    context, never in bulk «find all where X».

Enums (domain.enums):
  - Season — SUMMER / WINTER, with displayName() for UI.
  - SeasonalMode — MULTIPLIER (× base) / FIXED (override days).
  - SeasonalOverride — INHERIT / ON / OFF (per-plant decision).

User entity: 8 new fields with the obvious getters/setters via Lombok.
Plant entity: seasonalOverride field, defaulting to INHERIT for builder.

SeasonResolver:
  - currentSeason(user) — convenience for «now».
  - seasonAt(user, ZonedDateTime) — the testable variant. Resolves
    user's TZ via TimezoneSupport, computes MMDD as month*100+day, then
    delegates to classify().
  - classify(mmdd, summerStartMmdd, winterStartMmdd) is the pure
    integer-only function. Two cases:
    * summerStart <= winterStart (Northern hemisphere defaults):
      SUMMER iff mmdd ∈ [summerStart, winterStart).
    * summerStart > winterStart (Southern hemisphere / inverted):
      wrap-around — SUMMER iff mmdd >= summerStart OR mmdd < winterStart.

SeasonalIntervalService:
  - effectiveIntervalDays(plant, user, baseIntervalDays) — main entry
    point that integration code (commit 2/3) will use.
  - effectiveIntervalDaysAt(plant, user, base, when) — same with explicit
    time, for projection / tests.
  - isSeasonalActive(plant, user) — combines global setting with per-plant
    override. Treats null override as INHERIT for paranoia.
  - In MULTIPLIER mode: BigDecimal(base) × multiplier, scale=0 HALF_UP.
    null multiplier falls back to base.
  - In FIXED mode: returns the season's override-days if set, else base.
  - Result is always clamp(1..60) — per AC, prevents user-config disasters
    like 0-day cycles or 6-month silence.

Tests:
  - SeasonResolverTest, 13 cases via @ParameterizedTest covering both
    hemisphere modes and boundary dates (Apr 1, Sep 30, Oct 1, Mar 31).
    Plus 5 cases for the user-facing seasonAt with TZ awareness:
    July/December in Minsk, edge case where UTC and Asia/Tokyo land on
    different calendar days, and the season-start boundaries.
  - SeasonalIntervalServiceTest, 14 cases covering: combined active
    logic (5 cases — every cell of global × override matrix incl. null);
    MULTIPLIER mode (parameterized base/expected pairs incl. clamp at
    both ends); FIXED mode (override / fallback / clamp); disabled
    fast-path returning base; clamp still applies even with disabled.
